{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "JAS",
  "chapter": 2,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JAS.2.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.2.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My brethren, have not the faith of our Lord Jesus Christ, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "the Lord",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of glory, with respect of persons.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.2.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.2.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For if there come into your assembly a man with a gold ring, in goodly apparel, and there come in also a poor man in vile raiment;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.2.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.2.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And ye have respect to him that weareth the gay clothing, and say to him, Sit thou here in a good place; and say to the poor, Stand thou there, or sit here under my footstool:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.2.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.2.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Are ye not then partial in yourselves, and are become judges of evil thoughts?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.2.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.2.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hearken, my beloved brethren, Hath not God chosen the poor of this world rich in faith, and heirs of the kingdom which he hath promised to them that love him?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.2.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.2.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But ye have despised the poor. Do not rich men oppress you, and draw you before the judgment-seats?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.2.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.2.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Do they not blaspheme that worthy name by the which ye are called?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.2.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.2.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If ye fulfill the royal law according to the scripture, Thou shalt love thy neighbor as thyself, ye do well:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.2.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.2.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But if ye have respect to persons, ye commit sin, and are convicted by the law as transgressors.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.2.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.2.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For whoever shall keep the whole law, and yet offend in one ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "point",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", he is guilty of all.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.2.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.2.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For he that said, Do not commit adultery; said also, Do not kill. Now if thou committest no adultery, yet if thou killest, thou art become a transgressor of the law.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.2.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.2.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So speak ye, and so do, as they that shall be judged by the law of liberty.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.2.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.2.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For he shall have judgment without mercy that hath shown no mercy; and mercy rejoiceth against judgment.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.2.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.2.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "What ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "doth it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " profit, my brethren, though a man sayeth he hath faith, and hath not works? can faith save him?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.2.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.2.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If a brother or sister is naked, and destitute of daily food,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.2.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.2.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And one of you sayeth to them, Depart in peace, be you warmed and filled; notwithstanding ye give them not those things which are needful to the body; what ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "doth it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " profit?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.2.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.2.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Even so faith, if it hath not works, is dead, being alone.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.2.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.2.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Also a man may say, Thou hast faith, and I have works: show me thy faith without thy works, and I will show thee my faith by my works.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.2.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.2.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou believest that there is one God; thou doest well: the demons also believe, and tremble.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.2.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.2.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But wilt thou know, O vain man, that faith without works is dead?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.2.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.2.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Was not Abraham our father justified by works, when he had offered Isaac his son upon the altar?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.2.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.2.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Seest thou how faith wrought with his works, and by works was faith made perfect?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.2.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.2.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the scripture was fulfilled, which saith, Abraham believed God, and it was imputed to him for righteousness: and he was called the Friend of God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.2.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.2.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Ye see then that by works a man is justified, and not by faith only.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.2.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.2.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Likewise also was not Rahab the harlot justified by works, when she had received the messengers, and had sent ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " out another way?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.2.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.2.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For as the body without the spirit is dead, so faith without works is dead also.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
